                  \\big\rangle
                  \\;=\;
                  \\big\langle
                  \-
                  \\big\vert
                  \-
                  \\big\rangle
                  \\,,
          %p in that the induced projectivization
          #eq:ProjectivisedUnitaryOperator.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (4)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi P
                          %mi ℋ
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                              %mi U
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mtd
                          %mi P
                          %mi ℋ
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi ψ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↦
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} [
                          %mi U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi ψ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  P\mathcal{H}
                  \&amp;\xrightarrow{\;\;[U]\;\;}&amp;
                  P\mathcal{H}
                  \\\
                  [\psi]
                  \&amp;\mapsto&amp;
                  \\big[
                  U(\psi)
                  \\big]
                  }
          %p
            evidently satisfies
            = succeed "." do
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:QuantumSymmetry"} (3)
          %p
            On the one hand, there are more quantum symmetries than arise from unitary operators this way. Namely, if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anti-linear+map"} anti-linear
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anti-unitary+operator"} anti-unitary operator
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:ProjectivisedUnitaryOperator"} (4)
            still holds.
          %p
            On the other hand, this does now already exhaust the most general situation: Wigner’s theorem (Prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#WignerTheorem"}
            below) says that for every quantum symmetry
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi P
                  %mi ℋ
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi P
                  %mi ℋ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \,\colon\, P\mathcal{H} \xrightarrow{\;} P\mathcal{H}
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:QuantumSymmetry"} (3)
            there exists a map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi ℋ
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi ℋ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \,\colon\, \mathcal{H} \xrightarrow{\;} \mathcal{H}
            which is either a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitary+operator"} unitary operator
            or an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anti-unitary+operator"} anti-unitary operator
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \,=\, [U]
            = succeed "." do
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:ProjectivisedUnitaryOperator"} (4)
          %h2#Statement Statement
          %p
          #WignerTheorem.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              %strong (Wigner’s theorem)
              %br/
              Every quantum symmetry
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi P
                    %mi ℋ
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi P
                    %mi ℋ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \,\colon\, P\mathcal{H} \xrightarrow{\;} P\mathcal{H}
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:QuantumSymmetry"} (3)
              is the projectivization
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:ProjectivisedUnitaryOperator"} (4)
              of a map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi ℋ
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi ℋ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \,\colon\, \mathcal{H} \xrightarrow{\;} \mathcal{H}
              which is either a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitary+operator"} unitary operator
              or an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anti-unitary+operator"} anti-unitary operator
          The first full proof of this statement seems to be that due to
          = succeed "," do
            %a{:href => "#Bargmann64"} Bargmann 1964, §1.3
          = succeed "/" do
            %a{:href => "#Wigner31"} Wigner 1931
          = succeed "." do
            %a{:href => "#Wigner1959"} 59
          %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fubini-Study+metric"} Fubini-Study metric
          is given in
          = succeed "." do
            %a{:href => "#Freed12"} Freed 2012, Thm. 8
          %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pure+state"} pure
          %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+states"} quantum states
          is given in
          = succeed "." do
            %a{:href => "#Moretti17"} Moretti 2017, Thm. 12.11
          %h2#further_properties Further properties
          %div
            %h3#PCTQuantumSymmetries PCT Quantum Symmetries
            %p
              We discuss how
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/PCT+symmetry"} PCT
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+symmetries"} quantum symmetries
              (Def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PCTQuantumSymmetry"}
              below) are classified (Prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ClassificationOfPCTQuantumSymmetries"}
              below) by a “
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/10-fold+way"}> 10-fold way
              ” (Cor.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TenFoldWayOfPCTQuantumSymmetries"}
              below).
            %p
              The definition and the argument is quite straightforward. Just for completeness we offer some
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a{:href => "#PreliminariesForPCTQuantumSymmetries"} Preliminaries
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a{:href => "#PCTQuantumSymmetryDefinitionAndClassification"} Definition and Classification
            %p
              The 10-fold classification of these PCT quantum symmetries immediately induces other incarnations of the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/10-fold+way"} 10-fold way
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  the classification of flavors of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological K-theory
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KU-theory"}> KU-theory
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KO-theory"} KO-theory
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KR-theory"} KR-theory
                  in any degree)
                %p
                  (by the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Atiyah-J%C3%A4nich+theorem"} Atiyah-Jänich theorem
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "Atiyah-Jänich+theorem#SummaryInTermsOfGradedFredholmOperators"} in terms of graded Fredholm operators
            %p and with that
            %ul
              %li
                the 10-fold way in the
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory+classification+of+topological+phases+of+matter"} K-theory classification of topological phases of matter
            %h4#PreliminariesForPCTQuantumSymmetries Preliminaries
            %p Let:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi.mathscript ℋ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathscr{H}
                  be a countably infinite-dimensional
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert+space"} Hilbert space
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/U%28%E2%84%8B%29"}
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi.mathscript ℋ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{U}(\mathscr{H})
                  denote its
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitary+group"} unitary group
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                  be a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+structure"} real structure
                  on
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi.mathscript ℋ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathscr{H}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/antilinear+map"} antilinear
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/involution"} involution
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi C
                          %mn 2
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi t
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ≔
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mi id
                        %mo ,
                        %mi T
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_2^{(t)} \coloneqq \{id, T\}
                  denote the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cyclic+group+of+order+2"} group generated
                  by
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi T
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %p
              Observe that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semidirect+product"} semidirect product
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitary+group"} unitary group
              with that generated by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphic
              the group consisting of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitary+operators"} unitary operators
              %em and
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anti-unitary+operators"} anti-unitary operators
            #eq:GroupOfUnitaryAndAntiUnitaryOperators.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (5)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "center center center", :displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi.mathscript ℋ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ⋊
                          %msubsup
                            %mi C
                            %mn 2
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi t
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mo ∼
                        %mtd
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi.mathscript ℋ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ⊔
                          %msub
                            %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} U
                            %mi anti
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi.mathscript ℋ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi U
                          %mo ,
                          %mi id
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↦
                        %mtd
                          %mi U
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi U
                          %mo ,
                          %mi T
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↦
                        %mtd
                          %mi U
                          %mo ∘
                          %mi T
                          %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                            %mrow
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{array}{ccc}
                    \\mathrm{U}(\mathscr{H})
                    \\rtimes
                    C_2^{(t)}
                    \&amp;\overset{\sim}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    \\mathrm{U}(\mathscr{H})
                    \\sqcup
                    \\mathrm{U}_{anti}(\mathscr{H})
                    \\\
                    (U, id) &amp;\mapsto&amp; U
                    \\\
                    (U, T) &amp;\mapsto&amp; U \circ T
                    \\mathrlap{\,.}
                    \\end{array}
            %p
              This relation passes to
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+unitary+groups"} projective unitary groups
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi P
                            %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi.mathscript ℋ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≔
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi.mathscript ℋ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi P
                            %msub
                              %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} U
                              %mi anti
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi.mathscript ℋ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≔
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %msub
                              %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} U
                              %mi anti
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi.mathscript ℋ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    P \mathrm{U}(\mathscr{H})
                    \&amp;\coloneqq\;
                    \\mathrm{U}(\mathscr{H})/\mathrm{U}(1)
                    \\\
                    P \mathrm{U}_{anti}(\mathscr{H})
                    \&amp;\coloneqq\;
                    \\mathrm{U}_{anti}(\mathscr{H})/\mathrm{U}(1)
                    \\end{aligned}
            %p
              in that we have an analogous
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "center center center", :displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi P
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi.mathscript ℋ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ⋊
                          %msubsup
                            %mi C
                            %mn 2
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi t
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mo ∼
                        %mtd
                          %mi P
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi.mathscript ℋ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ⊔
                          %mi P
                          %msub
                            %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} U
                            %mi anti
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi.mathscript ℋ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mo ,
                          %mi id
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↦
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mo ,
                          %mi T
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↦
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi U
                          %mo ∘
                          %mi T
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                            %mrow
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{array}{ccc}
                    P \mathrm{U}(\mathscr{H})
                    \\rtimes
                    C_2^{(t)}
                    \&amp;\overset{\sim}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    P\mathrm{U}(\mathscr{H})
                    \\sqcup
                    P\mathrm{U}_{anti}(\mathscr{H})
                    \\\
                    ([U], id) &amp;\mapsto&amp; [U]
                    \\\
                    ([U], T) &amp;\mapsto&amp; [U \circ T]
                    \\mathrlap{\,.}
                    \\end{array}
            %p
              This group of
              %em projective unitary/antiunitary operators
              is the group of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+symmetries"} quantum symmetries
              as usually considered (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wigner%27s+theorem"}> Wigner's theorem
              ).
            %p
              We next enlarge this a little more to include what may be thought of as particle/antiparticle symmetry, often referred to as
              %em charge conjugation
              symmetry.
            %p To that end, let
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi.mathscript ℋ
                          %mi gr
                        %mo ≔
                        %mi.mathscript ℋ
                        %mo ⊖
                        %mi.mathscript ℋ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathscr{H}_{gr} \coloneqq \mathscr{H} \ominus \mathscr{H}
                  denote the
                  = succeed "-graded" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi ℤ
                            %mn 2
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}_2
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi P
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
                  the grading
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/involution"} involution
                  on
                  = succeed ":" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi.mathscript ℋ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathscr{H}
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mtable{:columnalign => "center center center", :displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi.mathscript ℋ
                            %mtd
                              %mover
                                %mo ⟶
                                %mi P
                            %mtd
                              %mi.mathscript ℋ
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mrow
                                %mo (
                                %mrow
                                  %mtable{:displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                                    %mtr
                                      %mtd
                                        %msub
                                          %mi ψ
                                          %mo +
                                    %mtr
                                      %mtd
                                        %msub
                                          %mi ψ
                                          %mo −
                                %mo )
                            %mtd
                              %mo ↦
                            %mtd
                              %mrow
                                %mo (
                                %mrow
                                  %mtable{:displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                                    %mtr
                                      %mtd
                                        %msub
                                          %mi ψ
                                          %mo −
